# x2_per_layer_disk: plaintext encoder layers wait on disk. Row three of the per-layer arm
# (bert_perlayer_disk_cpu.py). Donor: retired 02_per_layer 1,834 MB -> 03_disk_offload 1,322 MB.
#
# object     x1 holds the twelve BertLayer modules in a list (~469 MB float32) until use. Here each
#            layer's state_dict goes to disk at startup, model dropped, one layer rebuilt per turn, file
#            removed after read.
# trim       malloc_trim(0) after each gc.collect() is part of the lever (arena-held releases invisible
#            to RSS; plaintext_free_early_cpu: 433,255,432 B freed, peak unchanged).
# omitted    donor's MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2 (global allocator knob refused 17.08.: [heap] -1,044 MB, anon
#            +788 MB).
# free       no recomputation, arithmetic or round change; 469 MB disk written and read once.
# gate       identical to x1's expected (no generator consulted).
# expected   1,420,316 kB -> 1.05 to 1.15 GB (-20% to -25%); x1 spread 0.19%.
SHAFT_SCRIPT=$BASE/bert_perlayer_disk_cpu.py
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu,embed_chunk_cpu
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16"
